nd Internship Search Resources Information for Employers Join Handshake Play Watch the Video: High Tide Talks Watch the Video: High Tide Talks Hear one Flagler College student describe how the Career Development Center helped him get a killer internship - an important step toward the career he'll pursue after college. Career Development Tips Career Development Tips Unlock the keys to your future success with our valuable tips and guidance tailored to your aspirations and goals. Interview and Network Tips Resume and Cover Letter Tips Preparation for Graduate School Dress for Success The Forage - Find Your Career Path The Forage Trying to find and land a job after graduation is stressful and overwhelming, especially when you are already juggling a lot. That’s why we've partnered with Forage. Forage provides FREE virtual job simulations that walk you through a day in the life working in a specific role at a particular company. For example, you can try marketing at lululemon, investment banking at JPMorgan Chase, or customer service at Fidelity. You complete them on your own schedule, and once you’re done, you’re over 3x more likely to land a job! Forage helps you land a job by: Building new workplace skills you can add to your resume and talk about in interviews Demonstrating your interest to companies and standing out in the hiring pool Learning about different companies, industries, and career paths, so you feel confident when applying Getting access to resources that help you in the job search process, like resume templates, application tips, and interview guides The Forage Our Alumni Our Alumni Looking for some inspiration, or are you a past-graduate trying to connect with us? Check out our Alumni page at the link below for everything you may need. You can also check out our alumni map below to see where some of our graduates have started their businesses. Alumni Page Alumni-Owned Business View full-size map FC Grad Stories Flagler College graduates consistently reflect a lionhearted spirit defined by intelligence, creativity, skill, and entrepreneurship. Read the inspiring stories and future plans of our most recent graduates on our #FCGradStories pages. Find Out What's Next Flagler Senior Turns Passion for Science into Veterinary Future For Zoie Marchant, a senior double majoring in biology and coastal environmental science, a childhood curiosity about the ocean has grown into a clear path toward a career in veterinary medicine. Read Zoie's Story Design Week Tours Connect Students with Jacksonville’s Creative Industry Students traveled to Jacksonville for this year’s AIGA Design Week for behind-the-scenes tours of two leading creative agencies, Shepherd Advertising Agency and Wingard Marketing. Learn More About Design Week Alumni Businesses Return to Campus for Mini Mane Market The West Lawn transformed into a celebration of creativity and connection on Thursday as four alumni-owned businesses returned to campus for the Mini Mane Market, part of the larger Mane Event. Get a Glimpse of the Market Clubs, Orgs & Events - Why Getting Involved is a Game Changer Meet Our Team Meet Our Team Vernita Bowens Director of The Career Development Center VBowens@flagler.edu 904-826-8663 Read Vernita Bowens' thoughts on psychology careers in U.S. News  & World Reports' \"What Jobs Can You Get With a Psychology Degree?\" Explore Vernita's insights into great jobs for biology majors in another U.S. News & World Report story. Emily Palacios Career Success Coach EPalacios@flagler.edu 904-826-8761 Lauren DeFalco Employer Partnership Strategist LDefalco@flagler.edu 904-819-6353 Contact Us Contact Us If you have questions or would like to make an appointment, email us using the link below.  Faculty, staff, and organizations can also request a presentation. Email Us or Request a Presentation × Back to top of page Home Contact Us 74 King Street, St. Augustine, FL 32084 (904) 829-6481 admissions@flagler.edu Directions & Parking 74 King Street, St. A