    "https://www.flagler.edu/student-life/career-development-center/information-employers": {
      "title": "Signature Programs",
      "description": "Information for Employers | Flagler College Skip to main content Utility Visit Apply Deposit Give Contact News & Events Quick Links Academics Academics Degrees & Programs Graduate and Education Programs Signature Programs Flagler Core Center for Global Education Honors Program Undergraduate Research Community Integrative Education Center for Religion and Culture Academic Support Academic Access and Success Registrar Academic Catalog Proctor Library Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Visit Flagler Application Process First Year Applicants International Applicants Transfer Applicants Military & Veterans Applicants Living on Campus Admissions Team Tuition & Fees Cost Details Net Price Calculator Part-time, Graduate, Alumni, and Summer Tuition Residence Hall Costs Due Dates Admitted Students Financial Aid & Scholarships Federal Aid Financial Aid Process Financial Aid Team Grants Scholarships State Aid Apply Now Transfer Student Life Student Life Explore St. Augustine Living On Campus First Year Housing Sophomore Housing Junior/Senior Housing Types of Housing Dining Get Involved Groups & Clubs Student Government Health & Wellness Care Team Counseling Services Educational Initiatives Health Services Wellness Education Safety & Security Annual Security Report Emergency Information SafeSaints Program Career Development Career Assessment Four Year Career Plan Graduate School Preparation Information for Employers Interview and Networking Tips Job and Internship Search Resources Professional Attire Resume and Cover Letter Tips Student Spaces #FCGradStories 2025 About About Mission & Vision Our History Support Flagler Leadership Offices & Services Employee Directory Contact Us Athletics Explore Flagler Close Search Flagler.edu Sort by Relevance Authored on Title Main Academics Degrees & Programs Graduate and Education Programs Signature Programs Academic Support Academic Calendar Academic Projects Flagler College Tallahassee Legacy Admissions & Aid Visit Flagler Application Process Tuition and Fees Admissions Team Financial Aid & Scholarships Apply Now Transfer Your Credits Transfer to Flagler College Undecided Students News & Events Breaking Eggs Podcast History Maker in Residence Welcome Week Flagler News Presidential Speaker Series Publications Saints of NYC Saints of Atlanta The Mane Event WFCF Flagler College Radio About Mission & Vision Our History Support Flagler Leadership Office & Services Employee Directory Contact Us Flagler's Legacy Five-Star Plan Flagler Facts and Rankings Outcomes Student Life #FCGradStories 2026 Explore St. Augustine Two-Year Live-On Requirement at Flagler College Living On Campus Get Involved Health & Wellness Safety & Security Career Development Center Student Spaces Utility Mobile Apply Now Visit Deposit Give Athletics Flagler Forward Information for... Admitted Students Current Students Families Alumni Counselors Community Members Faculty & Staff Sites and Tools MyFlagler Saints Connect Canvas Academic Catalog Deposit Net Price Calculator Bookstore Proctor Library Parking Portal Planned Giving Mega Menu Footer Resources & Help Center Employee Directory Offices & Services Continuing Education Home Student Life Career Development Center Information For Employers Information for Employers Unlock Top Talent Jump to a Section... Flagler College is a thriving hub of emerging talent, poised to make a meaningful impact in the professional world. By connecting with us, employers gain access to a diverse pool of motivated and well-prepared students and graduates. Employers play a pivotal role in shaping students' career journeys, offering valuable perspectives and opportunities for growth. Discover how we can assist you in: Recruiting from a pool of exceptionally talented undergraduate students. Building connections with Flagler College academic departments and student organizations. Leveraging the expertise of our vast network of accomplished Flagler College alumni. Elevating your brand's presence and influence on our dynamic campus. Partner with Flagler College to tap into a pipeline of exceptional talent ready to contribute to your organization's success. Take a look below at some of the ways you can partner with Flagler College. On Campus Recruitment Opportunities On Campus Recruitment Opportunities Connect at Our Career Expos Flagler College hosts two Career Expos annually, one in the fall and another in the spring. These events provide an excellent opportunity to engage with a broader audience of students. Whether you're seeking part-time, or full-time hires, interns, or volunteers, our Career Expos offer a platform to promote your company's presence on campus and connect with potential talent. Don't miss your chance to make meaningful connections! Reserve a Table in High-Traffic Areas Secure a spot in our bustling student areas like Kenan Plaza or the Ringhaver Student Center. These prime locations offer access to students before and after their classes, ensuring you capture their attention as they move around the area. This exposure provides an excellent opportunity to connect with our students and promote your company effectively. Engage in Information Sessions Enhance your engagement with students by hosting information sessions, often accompanied by information tables. These intimate gatherings offer an opportunity for in-depth discussions with students interested in your company's opportunities. These sessions are held in our conference room, providing a conducive environment for meaningful conversations. On-Campus Interviews Made Easy Reserve our conference room to conduct on-campus interviews at your convenience. You have the flexibility to choose the interview duration, typically ranging from 20 minutes to one hour. We'll help promote the opportunity to our faculty and students, ensuring a pool of interested candidates for your consideration. Streamline your recruitment process with on-campus interviews at Flagler College. Just a Few Rules About Recruiting Here are a few policies to take note of: Recruiting Policy.pdf (75.75 KB) Fair Labor Standards Act.pdf (46.52 KB) Please Note Recruiting organizations and their representatives are expected to exercise their best efforts to follow the Principles for Employment Professionals set forth by the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE). How to Connect With Us How to Connect With Us As an employer, we'd love to connect you with one or many of our talented students. Register with Handshake - this will allow you to post jobs and events that directly get you in touch with our students Handshake Registration Contact Us - email us at careerdevelopment@flagler.edu or call us at 904-819-6286 × Back to top of page Home Contact Us 74 King Street, St. Augustine, FL 32084 (904) 829-6481 admissions@flagler.edu Directions & Parking 74 King Street, St. Augustine, FL 32084 (904) 829-6481 admissions@flagler.edu Directions & Parking Connect With Us Facebook Instagram Twitter Youtube Tiktok Newsletter Social Footer Facebook Instagram Twitter Youtube Tiktok Newsletter Flager Forward Popular Searches Degrees & Programs Living on Campus Take a Virtual Tour News & Events Graduate and Education Programs Popular Searches Degrees & Programs Living on Campus Take a Virtual Tour News & Events Graduate and Education Programs Let Us Help You Resources & Help Center Contact Employee Directory Careers Questions & Comments Let Us Help You Resources & Help Center Contact Employee Directory Careers Questions & Comments Flagler Forward Legal Footer © 2026 Flagler College. All rights reserved. Terms & Conditions Notice of Non-Discrimination Title IX Policies & Resources Flagler College Ease Grant Performance Measures"
