cy Admissions & Aid Visit Flagler Application Process Tuition and Fees Admissions Team Financial Aid & Scholarships Apply Now Transfer Your Credits Transfer to Flagler College Undecided Students News & Events Breaking Eggs Podcast History Maker in Residence Welcome Week Flagler News Presidential Speaker Series Publications Saints of NYC Saints of Atlanta The Mane Event WFCF Flagler College Radio About Mission & Vision Our History Support Flagler Leadership Office & Services Employee Directory Contact Us Flagler's Legacy Five-Star Plan Flagler Facts and Rankings Outcomes Student Life #FCGradStories 2026 Explore St. Augustine Two-Year Live-On Requirement at Flagler College Living On Campus Get Involved Health & Wellness Safety & Security Career Development Center Student Spaces Utility Mobile Apply Now Visit Deposit Give Athletics Flagler Forward Information for... Admitted Students Current Students Families Alumni Counselors Community Members Faculty & Staff Sites and Tools MyFlagler Saints Connect Canvas Academic Catalog Deposit Net Price Calculator Bookstore Proctor Library Parking Portal Planned Giving Mega Menu Footer Resources & Help Center Employee Directory Offices & Services Continuing Education Home Student Life Career Development Center Job and Internship Search Resources Job and Internship Search Resources Discover a wealth of invaluable resources and powerful tools at your disposal, all geared towards propelling you towards your dream internship or career. General Search Resources and Tools General Search Resources and Tools HandShake Your Handshake account is used to: Schedule an appointment with one of our career counselors Career Development events Job listings Internship opportunities Resume and cover letter guidance General Job Search Information CareerSHIFT enables job searchers to: Search, select, and store job listings from all job boards and all company job postings. Get up-to-date contact information, including e-mail addresses, for millions of companies. Access in-depth information about contacts and companies posting jobs. Record, save, and store your correspondence history records automatically. First Time Users must create a new account using a Flagler College email or Alumni email. Contact careerdevelopment@flagler.edu with any questions. Indeed The O*NETdatabase includes information on skills, abilities, work knowledge, activities, and interests associated with occupations. My Next Move site has tasks, skills, salary information, and more for over 900 different careers. The Occupational Outlook Handbook (OOH) is a career resource by the Bureau of Labor Statistics offering information on the hundreds of occupations that provide the overwhelming majority of jobs in the United States. Glassdoor holds a growing database of 6 million company reviews , CEO approval ratings, salary reports , interview reviews and questions, office photos, and more. USAJOBS is a job board enabling job seekers access to thousands of job opportunities across hundreds of federal agencies and organizations. Why Internships Matter Gain practical experience and first-hand exposure to the operations of an organization! By completing an internship, students will: Explore different career fields and industries Be more aware of professional duties and tasks required within specific areas Learn practical applications from in-class learning Add to your resumé Network with professionals and industry leaders Open the doors to future opportunities During the internship, an organization may request students to perform many duties to enlighten them about various aspects of the industry. All assignments should be related directly to the educational aspects of the internship. When a student and organization work together, it can provide a combination of work experiences and learning opportunities. The ultimate goal of an internship is to link theory to practice. (Cuneen & Sidwell, 1994, p. 47) When embarking on your quest for the perfect job, internship, or career path, the digital realm is your ally. Dive into a curated list of professional websites, thoughtfully selected to set you on the right track based on your academic major. Job Search Based On Major Job Search Based On Major Arts Ad Age Career Center Adweek Classifieds Agency Compile American Advertising Federation American Institute of Graphic Core77 / BusinessWeek Design Firm Directory Creative Hotlist Graphic Artists Guild Job Line HOW Job Bank IDSA Employment Museum, Non-Profit, Art Business Staffing SEGD Job Bank The Firm List Business 100 Careers in Wall Street HR Job Openings Marketing Classifieds Communication and Public Relations AT&T College Network Edelman Public Relations Worldwide Editor and Publisher Classified Public Relations Society of America Education Academic Employment Network Carney, Sandoe & Associates Chronicle of Higher Education Jobs Ed Week.org Higher Ed Jobs K-12 Education Jobs Master's Degree in Education Mission: Teach National Association of Independent Schools Southern Teachers Agency Teach for America Teachers-Teachers.com Top School Jobs Entertainment, Theater and Performing arts American Film Institute Association of Performing Arts Presenters Disney Entertainment Careers.Net Fox Entertainment Group LucasFilm LTD National Association of Broadcasters Center National Public Radio Internship Pixar Radio-Television Digital News Association Show Biz Jobs Universal Studios Paramount Warner Brothers Environmental American Planning Association Ecojobs.com EnviroLink Environmental Careers World Greenbiz.com Greenpeace Leed Certification Help National Wildlife Federation Texas A and M Job Board Outward Bound U.S. Environmental Protection Agency Government CIA Making the Difference U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics U.S. Department of State U.S. House of Representatives U.S. Justice Department U.S. Senate U.S. Treasury Department USA Jobs Humanities Advisory Council on Historic Preservation American Association for State and 