    "https://www.flagler.edu/student-life/career-development-center/resume-and-cover-letter-tips": {
      "title": "Signature Programs",
      "description": "Resume and Cover Letter Tips | Flagler College Skip to main content Utility Visit Apply Deposit Give Contact News & Events Quick Links Academics Academics Degrees & Programs Graduate and Education Programs Signature Programs Flagler Core Center for Global Education Honors Program Undergraduate Research Community Integrative Education Center for Religion and Culture Academic Support Academic Access and Success Registrar Academic Catalog Proctor Library Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Visit Flagler Application Process First Year Applicants International Applicants Transfer Applicants Military & Veterans Applicants Living on Campus Admissions Team Tuition & Fees Cost Details Net Price Calculator Part-time, Graduate, Alumni, and Summer Tuition Residence Hall Costs Due Dates Admitted Students Financial Aid & Scholarships Federal Aid Financial Aid Process Financial Aid Team Grants Scholarships State Aid Apply Now Transfer Student Life Student Life Explore St. Augustine Living On Campus First Year Housing Sophomore Housing Junior/Senior Housing Types of Housing Dining Get Involved Groups & Clubs Student Government Health & Wellness Care Team Counseling Services Educational Initiatives Health Services Wellness Education Safety & Security Annual Security Report Emergency Information SafeSaints Program Career Development Career Assessment Four Year Career Plan Graduate School Preparation Information for Employers Interview and Networking Tips Job and Internship Search Resources Professional Attire Resume and Cover Letter Tips Student Spaces #FCGradStories 2025 About About Mission & Vision Our History Support Flagler Leadership Offices & Services Employee Directory Contact Us Athletics Explore Flagler Close Search Flagler.edu Sort by Relevance Authored on Title Main Academics Degrees & Programs Graduate and Education Programs Signature Programs Academic Support Academic Calendar Academic Projects Flagler College Tallahassee Legacy Admissions & Aid Visit Flagler Application Process Tuition and Fees Admissions Team Financial Aid & Scholarships Apply Now Transfer Your Credits Transfer to Flagler College Undecided Students News & Events Breaking Eggs Podcast History Maker in Residence Welcome Week Flagler News Presidential Speaker Series Publications Saints of NYC Saints of Atlanta The Mane Event WFCF Flagler College Radio About Mission & Vision Our History Support Flagler Leadership Office & Services Employee Directory Contact Us Flagler's Legacy Five-Star Plan Flagler Facts and Rankings Outcomes Student Life #FCGradStories 2026 Explore St. Augustine Two-Year Live-On Requirement at Flagler College Living On Campus Get Involved Health & Wellness Safety & Security Career Development Center Student Spaces Utility Mobile Apply Now Visit Deposit Give Athletics Flagler Forward Information for... Admitted Students Current Students Families Alumni Counselors Community Members Faculty & Staff Sites and Tools MyFlagler Saints Connect Canvas Academic Catalog Deposit Net Price Calculator Bookstore Proctor Library Parking Portal Planned Giving Mega Menu Footer Resources & Help Center Employee Directory Offices & Services Continuing Education Home Student Life Career Development Center Resume and Cover Letter Tips Resume and Cover Letter Tips Your path to success begins with the right words on paper. Crafting an impressive resume and cover letter can significantly impact your career journey. These documents serve as your first introduction to potential employers, making it essential to master the art of presenting your skills and experiences effectively. Explore our expert tips and guidance to elevate your resume and cover letter, ensuring they stand out in the competitive job market. You can also view and download a sample resume and cover letter below. Resume Template.pdf (128.34 KB) Cover Letter Example.pdf (24.05 KB) Tips and Resources Tips and Resources Resume A resumé is a brief, detailed summary of your accomplishments in particular experiences. Keep it to one page unless you have significant experience to warrant two pages Use bullets when possible – they are easier and faster to read Every item on the resumé should be self-explanatory in how it relates to the position you are seeking. The reader should see the connections clearly. If an item needs further explanation you should remove or revise the item to make it clear to the reader. Quantify your experiences! This allows the reader to understand your abilities to be successful in other areas. Outline your successes, not simply stating job duties. Showcase how you used what you learned more than what you learned. See the measurement of your actual ability relevant to the task Stand out from other candidates who have done the same task with different results. Language and style showcase a professional image right from the start. Industry expressions show an understanding of the field. Use appropriate jargon for your audience. Begin your bullets with action verbs to emphasize strengths and qualifications. Use academic research and projects to exhibit further application in the field Research assistantships Senior seminar papers Capstone and group projects Cover Letter Writing an Effective Cover Letter: A Step-by-Step Guide A well-crafted cover letter is your opportunity to make a compelling case for why you're the ideal candidate for a job. Follow these steps to create a standout cover letter: Research: Learn about the company, its culture, and the job role. Tailor your cover letter to align with their values and requirements. Header: Include your contact information at the top, followed by the employer's details (if available). Salutation: Address the hiring manager by name whenever possible. If you don't have a name, use a generic greeting like \"Dear Hiring Manager.\" Opening Paragraph: Begin with a strong introduction that states the specific job you're applying for and how you learned about it. Express enthusiasm for the role and briefly highlight your qualifications. Body Paragraph(s): Provide evidence of your qualifications and relevant experiences. Connect your skills to the job requirements and showcase your achievements. Use specific examples to demonstrate your abilities. Customization: Tailor each cover letter to the specific job and company. Avoid generic templates; instead, personalize your letter for every application. Show Passion: Demonstrate your passion for the company and role. Explain why you're genuinely interested and how you align with their mission. Address Potential Concerns: If you have employment gaps or other potential red flags, address them briefly and positively. Closing Paragraph: Summarize your enthusiasm for the role and your desire to move forward in the hiring process. Express gratitude for the opportunity to apply. Signature: End with a professional closing (e.g., \"Sincerely\") and your typed name. Leave space for your physical signature if submitting a hard copy. Proofread: Carefully review your cover letter for spelling, grammar, and formatting errors. Consider asking a friend or career advisor for feedback. Formatting: Keep your cover letter clean and professional. Use a consistent font, size, and formatting style. Length: Aim for a one-page cover letter, keeping it concise and focused on your most relevant qualifications. Follow Instructions: If the job posting provides specific instructions for the cover letter, ensure you follow them precisely. Attachment: If submitting electronically, save your cover letter as a PDF to maintain formatting. Final Review: Before sending, double-check that your cover letter complements your resume and provides additional context for your qualifications. Remember, a well-crafted cover letter can set you apart from other applicants and demonstrate your genuine interest in the position. Customize each letter, showcase your qualifications, and showcase your passion for the role and company. Here's a visual guide to the information above. Cover Letter Guidelines.pdf (62.19 KB) Contact Us Contact Us If you have any questions about writing your resume or cover letter, please email us using the link below. Email Us × Back to top of page Home Contact Us 74 King Street, St. Augustine, FL 32084 (904) 829-6481 admissions@flagler.edu Directions & Parking 74 King Street, St. Augustine, FL 32084 (904) 829-6481 admissions@flagler.edu Directions & Parking Connect With Us Facebook Instagram Twitter Youtube Tiktok Newsletter Social Footer Facebook Instagram Twitter Youtube Tiktok Newsletter Flager Forward Popular Searches Degrees & Programs Living on Campus Take a Virtual Tour News & Events Graduate and Education Programs Popular Searches Degrees & Programs Living on Campus Take a Virtual Tour News & Events Graduate and Education Programs Let Us Help You Resources & Help Center Contact Employee Directory Careers Questions & Comments Let Us Help You Resources & Help Center Contact Employee Directory Careers Questions & Comments Flagler Forward Legal Footer © 2026 Flagler College. All rights reserved. Terms & Conditions Notice of Non-Discrimination Title IX Policies & Resources Flagler College Ease Grant Performance Measures"
